# Technical Specification: Intercom Smart Adapter (ESP32-C3 + Tuya/Matter)

This document describes the electrical schematic and software architecture for the in-unit Intercom Smart Adapter. Designed to fit inside a standard analog handset (e.g., Urmet CS1132), the module detects ringing signals via galvanic isolation, reports events to **Tuya Smart Life** over **Matter**, and opens the door latch on command from Tuya automations.

**Firmware:** [`intercom-adapter.ino`](intercom-adapter.ino)

> **v1 design rule:** The factory CA audio path is **never cut**. The adapter only **listens** (optocoupler tap) and **adds** door control (PhotoMOS in parallel). Custom ringback / CA injection is **out of scope** for v1 — see branch `matter-custom-audio`.

---

## 1. Core Concepts & Safety Isolation

The analog coordinate lines of multi-family buildings are sensitive. Bridging digital microcontrollers directly onto the bus presents serious risks:

- **Over-voltage:** Call lines carry 12 V AC – 24 V DC with switching spikes that destroy 3.3 V logic.
- **Line interference (Off-hook bug):** Drawing continuous power from audio lines drops bus impedance, locking the riser into a permanent "handset lifted" state.

### 1.1. Fail-Safe Principle (CA Never Cut)

The intercom must remain fully functional **without the adapter**:

| Function | v1 approach | If ESP is off / hung / no apartment power |
|----------|-------------|---------------------------------------------|
| Ring sound | Factory CA → buzzer path **unchanged** | Works (handset powered from riser) |
| Talk / listen | Factory PCB **unchanged** | Works |
| Door button | Factory pin 9–6 button **unchanged** | Works |
| Auto-open / app | PhotoMOS + Matter (additive) | Unavailable — expected |

The adapter is an **overlay**, not a single point of failure in the intercom signal path.

### 1.2. Galvanic Isolation (Optocoupler Guard)

Ring detection uses a **high-impedance parallel tap** on CA into a **PC817** optocoupler. The factory CA → buzzer route stays intact. The optocoupler provides a light barrier between the building bus and ESP32 GPIO.

