## 2. Electrical Schematic

### 2.1. System Overview

```
  CA (from riser)
       │
       ├──────────────────────────────────────> Factory buzzer path (DO NOT CUT)
       │
       └──> [1N4007] ── [10 µF] ── PC817 IN+ / IN− ──> GPIO4 (listen only)

  Pin 9 (lock) ──┬── Factory "Open" button ── Pin 6 (GND)
                 │
                 └── PhotoMOS OUT (parallel, normally open when idle)

  ESP32-C3: external 5 V PSU (NOT from intercom line)
```

### 2.2. Call Detector — Parallel Tap (AC Rectification & Filtering)

```
  CA ──────────┬────────────────────────────> To factory Urmet buzzer (unchanged)
               │
               └──────>| [1N4007] |---+---------------+
                                      |               |
                                      | +             |
                                      |-[Capacitor]   |----> IN+ (PC817 pin 1)
  Handset Pin 6 (GND) <────────────────| (10 µF 25V)  |
  (Common System Ground)               | -             |
                                      +--------------> IN− (PC817 pin 2)
```

**PC817 output → ESP32:**

| PC817 | Connection |
|-------|------------|
| Pin 3 (collector) | **GPIO4** (INPUT_PULLUP) |
| Pin 4 (emitter) | GND |
| Pull-up (internal) | 3.3 V via ESP32 INPUT_PULLUP |

Logic: active **LOW** during a call.

**Filter components:**
- **1N4007** — clips negative half-waves, protects optocoupler LED.
- **10 µF 25 V** — smooths 50 Hz ripple into stable DC during ringing.

**Wiring rule:** Solder the tap onto CA **before** or **alongside** the existing factory connection. Never remove the factory CA trace to the buzzer.

### 2.3. Automatic Door Release — PhotoMOS in Parallel (TLP172A)

PhotoMOS is wired **in parallel** with the handset "Open" button contacts. When idle (ESP off or GPIO low), outputs are open — the physical button works normally.

```
       ESP32-C3                                     PhotoMOS (TLP172A)
     +-----------+                                      +---------+
     |   GPIO2   |---------[ Resistor 220 Ω ]--------->| 1 (IN+) |
     |           |                                      |         |
     |    GND    |------------------------------------->| 2 (IN−) |
     +-----------+                                      |         |
                                                        | 3 (OUT) |──> Handset Pin 9 (Lock)
                                                        |         |
                                                        | 4 (OUT) |──> Handset Pin 6 (Ground)
                                                        +---------+
                              ║  (parallel with factory button on pin 9–6)
```

> **Pin note:** GPIO5/GPIO6 are reserved for the onboard 0.42" OLED (I2C). PhotoMOS uses **GPIO2**.

Door pulse: **2 s** active, then forced OFF in firmware.

### 2.4. OLED 0.42" Display (Onboard, SSD1306 72×40)

| Display | ESP32-C3 |
|---------|----------|
| VCC | 3.3 V |
| GND | GND |
| SDA | **GPIO5** |
| SCL | **GPIO6** |

Use **Software I2C** (U8g2 SW_I2C driver) — see generator spec §4 for snow/offset fix.

### 2.5. Custom Ringback — Not in v1

Cutting CA and injecting audio via BC547 makes the ring depend on ESP — rejected for production v1.

Future experiments (SPDT toggle, NC relay bypass): branch **`matter-custom-audio`**.

