## 4. Software Architecture (Tuya / Matter)

The adapter is **always-on** (external PSU + permanent Wi-Fi). ESP is always connected for ring detection and door control. **Schedule affects only auto-open logic** — not ring sound, not the physical door button.

### 4.1. On-Device Logic

| Step | Action |
|------|--------|
| Ring detected | GPIO4 goes LOW (parallel tap, factory audio unaffected) |
| Duration filter | Accept only 1.0 – 3.0 s (reject noise & stuck buttons) |
| Valid ring | Report **Contact Sensor** event to Matter → Tuya |
| Door open | **OnOff switch** endpoint; 2 s PhotoMOS pulse when triggered |

### 4.2. Tuya Automations

**Auto-open (working hours only):**

```
WHEN  Intercom Ring sensor → Open
IF    Time 16:00 – 20:00          ← schedule: auto-open ONLY
THEN  Intercom Door switch → ON
      (optional) Phone notification
```

**Manual open from app (always):**

```
WHEN  Tap "Open door" in Smart Life   ← no time condition
THEN  Intercom Door switch → ON
```

**Outside working hours:** ring sounds normally (factory buzzer), physical button works, app open works, **auto-open does not run**.

All schedule logic lives in the Tuya app. No NTP, no RTC, no on-device clock.

### 4.3. OLED Display States

| State | Screen |
|-------|--------|
| Boot / idle | `READY` + `TUYA OK` + `WiFi OK` |
| Commissioning | `PAIRING...` / `Smart Life` |
| Ring active | `>>> RING <<<` + duration timer |
| Event sent | `EVENT SENT` → `Tuya` |
| Door opening | `DOOR OPEN` + progress bar |
| No network | `NO WiFi` (ring & button still work) |

