## 5. Fail-Safe & Degraded Operation

| Condition | Ring | Handset button | App / auto-open |
|-----------|------|----------------|-----------------|
| ESP hung | ✅ factory | ✅ | ❌ until reboot |
| No apartment 220V | ✅* | ✅* | ❌ (ESP unpowered) |
| No Wi-Fi | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |
| Normal, outside schedule | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ app, ❌ auto |

\*Handset typically powered from building riser, not apartment mains.

**Firmware recommendations:** watchdog timer, no long blocking delays, force PhotoMOS OFF in `setup()`.

**Hardware rules:** never cut CA; never replace lock button with PhotoMOS only; never power ESP from intercom line.

---

## 6. Power & Connectivity Constraints

**Power stealing is forbidden.** The ESP32-C3 draws up to 350 mA during Wi-Fi TX — far beyond what the intercom line can supply (~1–2 mA). Use an external 5 V PSU (mini AC/DC module in the junction box).

**Always-on mode.** Deep sleep is not used: Wi-Fi must stay connected for Matter event delivery to Tuya.

---

## 7. Flashing

1. Open [`intercom-adapter.ino`](intercom-adapter.ino) in Arduino IDE.
2. Board: **ESP32C3 Dev Module**.
3. Install libraries: **Arduino Matter**, **U8g2**.
4. Flash via USB (disconnect from intercom wiring first).
5. Commission in **Smart Life** app (Matter pairing).
6. Create Tuya automations: auto-open (with time condition) + manual app open.
